.TH "ROARK\-CHAT\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-chat-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-chat\-create \- Create a chat
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark chat create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Create a new chat with segments (messages and tool invocations)
.SH "API"
POST /v1/chat
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-timestamp\fR \fI<value>\fR
When the chat started (ISO 8601 format) Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-timestamp\fR \fI<value>\fR
When the chat ended (ISO 8601 format) Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-messages\fR \fI<value>\fR
Ordered list of messages exchanged during the chat Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-tool\-invocations\fR \fI<value>\fR
List of tool invocations made during the chat Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-properties\fR \fI<value>\fR
Custom properties to include with the chat. These can be used for filtering and will show in the chat details page Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional OpenTelemetry trace ID for the chat. Surfaces the chat in the tracing tab. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-external\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
A stable identifier from your own system (e.g. session ID, conversation ID) used to correlate this chat with OpenTelemetry traces. Set the same value as a `roark.external_id` span or resource attribute on your traces and the matching trace will be linked automatically. Must be unique within a project. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fI<value>\fR
Single agent participating in the chat. Use this for the simpler API when you have only one agent. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent.prompt\fR \fI<value>\fR
Agent's prompt configuration (optional) Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-agents\fR \fI<value>\fR
Agents participating in the chat. Each agent requires identification and prompt information. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-customer\fR \fI<value>\fR
Single customer participating in the chat. Use this for the simpler API when you have only one customer. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-customer.label\fR \fI<value>\fR
Label to identify this customer in the chat (e.g., "user\-01", "anonymous\-visitor") Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-customer.phone\-number\-e164\fR \fI<value>\fR
Customer phone number in E.164 format (e.g., +14155551234), optional for chat customers Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-customers\fR \fI<value>\fR
Customers participating in the chat. Optional.
